{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2019-10-25 22:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E SAYS NEARLY ALL CUSTOMERS IMPACTED BY POWER SAFETY SHUTOFFS ON OCT 23 RESTORED', 'text': 'OCT 25  - PG&E CORP <PCG.N>::PSPS UPDATE FOR OCT. 23 SHUTOFF EVENT: NEARLY ALL CUSTOMERS IMPACTED BY POWER SAFETY SHUTOFFS RESTORED.PG&E CONTINUES TO MONITOR POTENTIALLY STRONG, WIDESPREAD OFFSHORE WIND EVENT OVER WEEKEND.99% OF CUSTOMERS IMPACTED BY PUBLIC SAFETY POWER SHUTOFF (PSPS) ON OCTOBER 23 HAD THEIR POWER RESTORED AS OF 5 P.M. TODAY..APPROXIMATELY 178,000 CUSTOMERS WERE ORIGINALLY IMPACTED BY THIS PSPS FROM SIERRA FOOTHILLS TO NORTH BAY TO SAN MATEO AND KERN COUNTIES.TO DATE, PG&E HAS CONFIRMED 7 INSTANCES OF WIND-RELATED DAMAGE AND HAZARDS TO ITS SYSTEM IN PSPS-IMPACTED AREAS.'}